# Departments that declare neither a `retry` policy nor `wrap_pipeline_failure`, so a thrown
# error is ACKed as `dropped_no_retry_policy` with no failure fact and no dead letter
# (fkst-substrate crates/fkst-framework/src/supervise/consumer.rs:702-710).
#
# Format: <package>.<department>|issue=#N|why=<one-line reason>
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. New entries fail CI. Remove an entry by giving the department a `retry` policy
# or `wrap_pipeline_failure` -- never by widening the structural exemptions in
# scripts/check_repo_dept_failure_surface.py.
#
# `dead_letter` and `test_*` departments are structurally exempt by role and are not listed.
github-devloop.liveness_scan|issue=#2996|why=liveness sweep drives every stuck-state redrive; a throw from replay_fixing vanishes here. Highest priority to remove.
github-devloop-pr.liveness_scan|issue=#2996|why=same sweep on the PR side; this is the path that produced PR#2915's 39h redrive/skip loop. Highest priority to remove.
archaudit.audit|issue=#2996|why=inventoried at ratchet introduction; throw-reachability not yet audited.
